{{see|pita}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
Usually pronounced as the noun ''[[pita]]'' with more emphasis on second sylable (peh-TAH instead of pee-tah).

===Noun===
'''PITA'''

# {{context|acronym}} PITA is an initialism or acronym for "pain in the ass". It is often used informally for a person the speaker finds troublesome, but can also refer to a nagging problem, or any task that is more awkward and complicated than it should be.

# {{context|acronym}} PITA - Computer file name extension used to ensure that e-mail attachments reach the intended recipients.  Executable file name extensions (.exe, .cmd,.bat...) and other files blocked by e-mail systems are renamed to .pita by the sender . When the recipient recieves the e-mail, the file can be detached and renamed with its original extension.
The origin of pita is due to blocked files being deemed a "pain in the arse".Note "Arse", not "Ass" - this usage is of Uk origin.

''"I've attached the batch job as a pita. just rename it to .bat"''